0..76 Comment "// Confluence certificates as paths in a presented type, and univalence over"
77..153 Comment "// the types of them (the HoTT book\'s § 2.10; Behr and Kock, _Tracelet Hopf"
154..231 Comment "// Algebras and Decomposition Spaces_, EPTCS 372, 2022). The critical pair of"
232..308 Comment "// the presented integers at `S(P(S(x)))` joins at `S(x)` two ways, and each"
309..383 Comment "// way is a certificate: a path from the peak to the join. The two are one"
384..459 Comment "// path, so certificate identity is an identification in the presented type"
460..536 Comment "// rather than a relation beside it; certificates no rule relates stay apart"
537..615 Comment "// (the pathological twin). Two boundaries that convert have certificate types"
616..688 Comment "// that `ua` makes one, and a consumer of one boundary\'s certificates is"
689..725 Comment "// carried to the other\'s unchanged."
727..762 Comment "// The presented integers and `up`."
